;; templating, itself, is a sort of aliasing.
;; so the stunts in this file aren't terribly useful.
;; we'll see more useful cases later with composite type constructors.

#|

Test disabled due to  This test fails due to a macro visibility issue 
where the generated GEN-NAME macro is not immediately visible 
to subsequent forms in the same file during compilation. 
This is an edge case specific to immediate usage of generated macros;

(with-template-type (T)
  (def-type some-float T))

(gen-some-float half)

(def-function scale (a b)
    (declare #'(some-float some-float => some-float))
    (/ (* a (to some-float 100.0)) b))

|#